# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Environments / secrets ---
.env
.env.local

# --- Lean ---
.lake/
lake-packages/
lakefile.olean
*.olean
*.ilean

# --- Data, indices, checkpoints: large and regenerable, never committed ---
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. `data/` (no slash) matches a directory named `data` at ANY depth,
# which silently excluded `src/prooflens_prover/data/` -- the benchmark and premise-corpus loaders --
# from every commit. The package imported fine locally because the files were on disk; a fresh
# clone raised `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'prooflens_prover.data'`. Caught by the CSF3
# gate, which is the only place the repo is ever exercised as a clone.
/data/
/indices/
*.jsonl
# COMMENTS MUST BE ON THEIR OWN LINE. Git only treats `#` as a comment at the START of a line, so a
# trailing comment becomes part of the pattern and the rule silently matches nothing. Both
# negations below were written with trailing comments and neither worked: the exported run records
# were excluded from the commit that was supposed to publish them, and the fixture whitelist had
# been dead since it was written (latent only because no fixture existed yet).
# Tiny bundled fixtures DO ship, so tests run on a fresh clone:
!tests/fixtures/**/*.jsonl
# Distilled run records (traces stripped) — every published number is recomputable from these:
!results/exported/**/*.jsonl
*.npy
*.faiss
*.safetensors
*.bin
results/checkpoints/
results/logs/

# --- Cluster noise ---
slurm-*.out
slurm-*.err

# --- Results that DO ship (tables + figures) are whitelisted above by omission ---

# --- Working notes that are NOT part of the published artefact ---
# The repo publishes what is needed to run and reproduce, plus README.md. Supervision notes are
# written for one meeting and go stale immediately; shipping them would put a half-current summary
# next to the maintained one and leave a reader to guess which is authoritative.
MEETING.md
dissertation.md
# Transfer staging: extracted cluster exports and copies of the benchmark files. Everything here
# is a copy of something authoritative elsewhere, so committing it would create a second source
# of truth for numbers that must come from results/exported.
/scratch/
exported.tgz

# --- Editors / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
